menu "Factory recovery boot"

    config FACTORY_RECOVERY_BOOT_GPIO
        int "GPIO used to request factory recovery"
        range 0 61 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32S31
        default 7
        help
            The bootloader configures this pin as an input with its internal
            pull-up enabled. Holding it low during reset selects the factory
            recovery image for this boot only.

    config FACTORY_RECOVERY_BOOT_DEBOUNCE_MS
        int "Low-level debounce time (milliseconds)"
        range 0 1000
        default 50
        help
            The pin must remain low for this duration. A released pin adds no
            debounce delay to normal startup.

    config FACTORY_RECOVERY_LONG_PRESS_GPIO
        int "GPIO used to request factory recovery by long press"
        range 0 61 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32S31
        default 57
        help
            The bootloader only reads this pin, with its internal pull-up
            enabled, and never drives it. Holding it low for the long-press
            time during reset selects the factory recovery image for this boot
            only.

    config FACTORY_RECOVERY_LONG_PRESS_MS
        int "Long-press time (milliseconds)"
        range 0 3000
        default 300
        help
            The long-press pin must remain low for this duration after the boot
            splash is shown. Releasing it earlier continues the normal boot. A
            released pin adds no delay to normal startup.

endmenu
